## Pattern
Use MSW to intercept network requests in tests:
```typescript
import { setupServer } from 'msw/node';
import { http, HttpResponse } from 'msw';

const server = setupServer(
  http.get('/api/agents', () => {
    return HttpResponse.json([
      { name: 'test-agent', description: 'A test agent' }
    ]);
  }),
  http.post('/api/agents', async ({ request }) => {
    const body = await request.json();
    return HttpResponse.json({ ...body, id: 'new-id' }, { status: 201 });
  })
);

beforeAll(() => server.listen());
afterEach(() => server.resetHandlers());
afterAll(() => server.close());
```

## Advantage
MSW works at the network level, so it tests the full request/response cycle including serialization.

